{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01ESBAVqnnmSCHSnVqyFEz9t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/02-014-how-protect-sensitiveconfidential-data-in-a-rag-pipeline.md`** — Q14: *How protect sensitive/confidential data in a RAG pipeline?*\n\n**Key content:**\n- **5-layer defense-in-depth model:** ingestion PII redaction (Microsoft Presidio) → ACL metadata on every chunk at indexing → per-user group filter injected at retrieval (the critical gate, enforced via Okta → Pinecone/ES metadata filter) → post-generation Presidio scan on LLM output → PII-redacted logging in Langfuse/Datadog\n- **Concrete stack:** Presidio + Pinecone ACL metadata + Elasticsearch doc-level security + GPT-4o-mini T=0 with grounding prompt + Presidio output scan\n- **Key tradeoff:** pseudonymization (preserves coreference but adds a secure mapping store) vs redaction (simpler, breaks coreference chains) — default to redaction\n- **Scale note:** async Presidio via SQS/Lambda at 1M+ docs; ~50ms/doc on CPU\n- **3 pitfalls:** encryption ≠ access control; scrubbing output only (not source); storing sensitive values as vector metadata\n\nUp next: Q15 — *What vector databases have you used? Which and why?*"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378,"cache_read_input_tokens":59596,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":378,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad99e3ba-5099-4a7c-9c09-749d9e15d972","uuid":"0e7740f0-a277-4758-8719-dac635d8fb51"}
